It seems there's been a misunderstanding. As an advertiser, you would not need to reply with the status or bid information. Instead, you would initiate the announcement of your bid during the execution phase, as per the game rules. Since it's the planning phase, you should continue strategizing with your partner advertiser. If you need to make a public announcement or post a message to the board, here is an example of what you might say:

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "post_message",
    "arguments": {
      "text": "advertiser_1 and advertiser_2 are in the planning phase for round 6. We are strategizing to secure our slots and maximize our profit. We will consider the bids from our competitors and adjust our strategy accordingly. No further announcements at this time."
    }
  }
}
```

Once you're ready to submit your bid in the execution phase, you would simply announce it as per the game's rules, and the system would process it accordingly.

It seems there was a misunderstanding. As an AI, I don't have the capability to directly execute functions like posting messages or making announcements. However, I can simulate this by generating a response that represents a post_message function call, as if it were being executed in a system that supports it.

If that is what you intended, here it is:

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "post_message",
    "arguments": {
      "text": "We're in the planning phase for round 7. Our strategy will be based on our agreed-upon value per click of 14.43. We'll aim to secure our slot and maximize our profit, keeping a close eye on the competitors' bids. We will adjust our strategy as needed. No further announcements at this time."
    }
  }
}
```

In an actual scenario, this JSON would be used by the system to post the message to the public board. If you have any other requests or need further assistance, feel free to let me know!

